          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %strong De Morganization
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℰ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
            is a universal way to turn
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℰ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
            into a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Morgan+topos"} de Morgan topos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Sh
                    %mi m
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℰ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh_m(\mathcal{E})
            with the use of a certain
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lawvere-Tierney+topology"} Lawvere-Tierney topology
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi m
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m
            %strong De Morgan topology
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
          %p
            This can be viewed as an analogue to the Booleanization
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Sh
                    %mrow
                      %mo ¬
                      %mo ¬
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℰ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh_{\neg\neg}(\mathcal{E})
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℰ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
            with the help of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+negation"} double negation topology
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ¬
                  %mo ¬
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \neg\neg
            \.
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℰ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
            be a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
            %em De Morgan topology
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi m
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℰ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
            is defined as the smallest
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lawvere-Tierney+topology"} Lawvere-Tierney topology
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi j
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j
            such that the canonical monomorphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo ⊤
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ⊥
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ↣
                  %msub
                    %mi Ω
                    %mrow
                      %mo ¬
                      %mo ¬
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\top,\bot): 1\coprod 1\rightarrowtail \Omega_{\neg\neg}
            is
            = succeed "-dense." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j
            %em De Morganization
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℰ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
            is the associated topos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Sh
                    %mi m
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℰ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh_m(\mathcal{E})
            of
            = succeed "-sheaves." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi m
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m
          %h3#remark Remark
          %p
            Here
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Ω
                    %mrow
                      %mo ¬
                      %mo ¬
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega_{\neg\neg}
            denotes the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobject+classifier"} subobject classifier
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Sh
                    %mrow
                      %mo ¬
                      %mo ¬
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℰ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh_{\neg\neg}(\mathcal{E})
            with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ¬
                  %mo ¬
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \neg\neg
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+negation"} double negation topology
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi m
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m
            is well-defined due to
            %em Joyal’s lemma
            (cf.
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Johnstone77"} Johnstone 1977
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Johnstone"} Johnstone 2002
            %a{:href => "double+negation#smallest_j-dense"} proposition
            about
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Sh
                    %mrow
                      %mo ¬
                      %mo ¬
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℰ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh_{\neg\neg}(\mathcal{E})
            \.
          %h2#example Example
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              The De Morganization of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+topos"} classifying topos
              for the theory of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} fields
              is the classifying topos for the geometric theory of fields of finite characteristic, in which every element is algebraic over the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prime+field"} prime field
          %p
            This is proposition 2.3 in
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#CJ09"} Caramello-Johnstone (2009)
          %h2#properties Properties
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              The De Morgan topology
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi m
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dense+subtopos"} smallest dense topology
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
              , i.e.
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                    %mo ≤
                    %mo ¬
                    %mo ¬
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j\leq \neg\neg
              , such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Sh
                      %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh_j(\mathcal{E})
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/De+Morgan+topos"} De Morgan topos
          %p
            This appears as theorem 1 in
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Caramello09"} Caramello (2009)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Sh
                    %mi m
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℰ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh_{m}(\mathcal{E})
            is the
            %em largest dense De Morgan subtopos
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℰ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
          #DeMorgan_mono.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              The De Morgan topology
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi m
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m
              is the smallest
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lawvere-Tierney+topology"} topology
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
              such that all monomorphisms of the form
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ¬
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∨
                    %mo ¬
                    %mo ¬
                    %mi A
                    %mo ↣
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \neg A\vee\neg\neg A\rightarrowtail E
              for subobjects
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ↣
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\rightarrowtail E
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
              are
              = succeed "-dense." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi j
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j
          %p
            This appears as proposition 6.2 in
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Caramello12a"} Caramello (2012a)
          #DeMorgan_prop.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_4 Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi m
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m
              be the De Morgan topology on it.
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Sh
                          %mi m
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi ℰ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mi ℰ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh_m(\mathcal{E})=\mathcal{E}
                  iff
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℰ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
                  is a
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/De+Morgan+topos"} De Morgan topos
              %li
                %p
                  For any
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dense+subtopos"} dense topology
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi j
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j
                  on
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℰ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
                  ,
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi Sh
                            %mi m
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi Sh
                            %mi j
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi ℰ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo =
                          %msub
                            %mi Sh
                            %mrow
                              %mi m
                              %mo ∨
                              %mi j
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi ℰ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh_m(Sh_j(\mathcal{E}))=Sh_{m\vee j}(\mathcal{E})
          %p
            %a{:href => "#Caramello09"}> Caramello (2009)
            , prop.1.5. In fact, in the second statement it suffices to demand that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi j
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weakly+open+topology"} weakly open topology
            i.e. the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associated+sheaf+functor"} associated sheaf functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mi j
                  %mo :
                  %mi ℰ
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi Sh
                    %mi j
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℰ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a_j:\mathcal{E}\to Sh_j(\mathcal{E})
            preserves the pseudo-complementation operator in the lattices of subobjects (cf.
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Caramello12"} Caramello (2012, prop.4.5)
          %p
            Notice that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Sh
                    %mrow
                      %mi m
                      %mo ∨
                      %mi j
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℰ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi Sh
                    %mi m
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℰ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∩
                  %msub
                    %mi Sh
                    %mi j
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℰ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh_{m\vee j}(\mathcal{E})=Sh_{m}(\mathcal{E})\cap Sh_{ j}(\mathcal{E})
            and, accordingly, for a dense or, more generally a weakly open subtopos De Morganization simply amounts to intersection with
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Sh
                      %mi m
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh_m(\mathcal{E})
          %h2#geometric_morphisms_preserving_de_morganizations Geometric morphisms preserving De Morganizations
          %p
            Notice that in analogy to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Sh
                    %mrow
                      %mo ¬
                      %mo ¬
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℰ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh_{\neg\neg}(\mathcal{E})
            and the class of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/skeletal+geometric+morphism"} skeletal geometric morphism
            %strong m-skeletal geometric morphisms
            as those geometric morphisms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi ℱ
                  %mo →
                  %mi ℰ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:\mathcal{F}\to\mathcal{E}
            that restrict to geometric morphisms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi m
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi Sh
                    %mi m
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℱ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi Sh
                    %mi m
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℰ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f|_m:Sh_m(\mathcal{F})\to Sh_m(\mathcal{E})
            \.
          %p
            Due to a result in
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Johnstone"} Johnstone (2002, p.194)
            = succeed "-dense" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi m
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^\ast
          %p
            By the
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#DeMorgan_prop"} above proposition
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Sh
                    %mi m
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi Sh
                    %mi j
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℰ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↪
                  %msub
                    %mi Sh
                    %mi m
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℰ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh_m(Sh_{j}(\mathcal{E}))\hookrightarrow Sh_{m}(\mathcal{E})
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi j
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j
            dense. Accordingly,
            %em dense inclusions
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Sh
                    %mi j
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℰ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi ℰ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh_{j}(\mathcal{E})\hookrightarrow\mathcal{E}
            are m-skeletal !
          %p
            The
            %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/skeletal+geometric+morphism#Boolean_skeletal"} characterization of Boolean toposes by skeletal morphisms
            carries over to m-skeletal morphisms and De Morgan toposes:
          #DeMorgan_m-skeletal.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_5 Proposition
            %p
              A topos
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
              is De Morgan iff every geometric morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℱ
                    %mo →
                    %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{F}\to\mathcal{E}
              is m-skeletal.
          %p
            %strong> Proof
            \: Assume
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℰ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
            is De Morgan, then it coincides with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Sh
                    %mi m
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℰ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh_m(\mathcal{E})
            and
            = succeed "-sheaves" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi m
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℱ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{F}
            necessarily have to land there.
          %p
            Conversely, assume all
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℱ
                  %mo →
                  %mi ℰ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{F}\to\mathcal{E}
            are m-skeletal. Then the surjective morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi γ
                  %mi ℰ
                  %mo →
                  %mi ℰ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:\gamma\mathcal{E}\to\mathcal{E}
            from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/De+Morgan+topos"} Gleason cover
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi γ
                  %mi ℰ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma\mathcal{E}
            is m-skeletal. But
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi γ
                  %mi ℰ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma\mathcal{E}
            is De Morgan and, therefore, so is
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi im
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} im(f)=\mathcal{E}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ▪
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \qed
